; axelf.vtms — "Axel F" (Harold Faltermeyer) opening synth hook.
;
; Lead melody transcribed from the 8bitpeoples/Yuppster C64 SID cover
; (~/Music/C64Music/DEMOS/A-F/Axel_F.sid), by rendering it with sidplayfp
; and pitch-tracking the result (FFT peak-picking with parabolic sub-bin
; interpolation, sampled mid-note rather than at the onset transient) rather
; than trusting memory. Lands cleanly on a G natural minor scale
; (G-Bb-C-D-Eb-F), which is a good sign the note-by-note reads are right —
; an earlier pass that sampled right at each onset picked up several wrong
; (chromatic, out-of-scale) notes from attack-transient bleed.
; Covers the opening riff plus its resolving tail (G4-F4-F4-D4-A4, ~4.15s-
; 5.0s) that leads back into the loop point. After that the SID holds a
; single sustained/PWM-textured G4 for ~2.4s (not a note sequence — the
; pitch never moves, just a slow timbral pulse we have no way to reproduce
; in this format) before a second, different melodic phrase; neither of
; those is transcribed here. Bass/hat/kick are a plain accompaniment (a
; G-2 pedal + steady hat/kick), not extracted from the SID's actual
; bassline — that band was too noisy to pitch-track reliably.
;
; Compile with:
;   python3 ../tools/vtm_compile.py axelf.vtms AXELF.VTM
; Then copy AXELF.VTM onto your test disk renamed to DEMO.VTM (test_player.c
; loads that name), or edit test_player.c's filename to match.

TEMPO 6
LOOP 0

INSTRUMENT 0 WAVE=PULSE PW=24 VOL=63 PAN=LR DECAY=3   ; lead "clav" hook — slight pluck
INSTRUMENT 1 WAVE=TRIANGLE PW=0 VOL=63 PAN=LR DECAY=5 ; bass pluck — smooth fade, no hard cutoff click
INSTRUMENT 2 WAVE=NOISE PW=48 VOL=32 PAN=LR DECAY=10  ; hat — quick tick
INSTRUMENT 3 WAVE=NOISE PW=4  VOL=48 PAN=LR DECAY=8   ; kick — short thud

PATTERN 0
G-4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
...    ...    ...    ...
...    ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
A#4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
...    ...    G-4:2  ...
G-4:0  ...    ...    ...
...    G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
...    ...    ...    ...
C-5:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
G-4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
F-4:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
G-4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
...    ...    ...    ...
...    ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
D-5:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
...    ...    G-4:2  ...
G-4:0  ...    ...    ...
...    G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
G-4:0  ...    ...    ...
D#5:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
D-5:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
A#4:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
G-4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
...    ...    ...    ...
D-5:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
G-5:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
G-4:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
F-4:0  ...    ...    ...
...    G-2:1  G-4:2  A-2:3
F-4:0  ...    ...    ...
D-4:0  ...    G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...
A-4:0  G-2:1  G-4:2  ...
...    ...    ...    ...

ORDER 0
